E63 draft — kolt's server onto the full-stack ladder (rung 1 + rung 0+)
=======================================================================

A PROPOSAL, not an applied change. The kolt checkout was read and nothing in
it was modified; no git command was run there. Apply with:

    cd <your kolt checkout> && git apply /path/to/kolt-server.patch

Everything above the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

SCOPE — deliberately narrow

`src/server.vl` is 289 lines and only the boot/shell/asset part moves. The
SQLite schema, the pbkdf2 externs, the module-level `Database`, all seven
closures behind `KoltStore`, `session_user`, `load_tasks`, `load_workspaces`
and `open_session` are untouched, byte for byte. The rpc protocol moves to
`.with_service(…)`; everything else stays exactly where it is.

WHAT MOVES

  - The three boot reads (`dist/client.js`, `dist/client.css`,
    `src/app.html`) become `require_build("client")` +
    `require_shell("src/app.html", build)`. No `dist/` path and no MIME type
    is spelled in this file any more, so renaming the client leg cannot
    leave it compiling and the page blank.
  - The three-arm `match request.path()` becomes `.serve_build(build)`: one
    route per artifact the build wrote, content type from the extension. If
    the client leg ever gains `split = true`, its chunk routes appear with
    no edit here at all.
  - `serve_service(59401, protocol, fallback, on_ready)` becomes a
    `Server::builder()` chain with `.with_service(Service::new(protocol))`.
    Same routes, same wire — `serve_service` has been a four-line body over
    this layer since v0.34.0 — but the page and the service now compose, so
    adding a second service later is `.with_service(…).at("/admin/")` rather
    than a rewrite of the boot function.
  - `src/app.html` is KEPT and unchanged. `require_shell` reads it once at
    boot and holds it against the build: a `<link>` for a stylesheet the
    build no longer emits, a `<script>` naming a renamed bundle, a mount
    `<div id>` that drifted from `mount_root` — each stops the server,
    naming the file and the fix, instead of serving a page that renders
    wrong and looks right. Rung 2 (`Document::of(build).title("Kolt (vilan
    pilot)")`, and the file goes away) is available and your shell is plain
    enough for it, but it would add `lang="en"` and a viewport meta the
    current shell does not carry — a served-bytes change under e2e/run.sh,
    which is why this draft does not take it.

Counted by fullstack-dx.md §1.2's rule (non-blank, non-comment lines):
248 → 249 lines, and 10 ceremony lines become 7. The count rises by one
because the builder chain puts each call on its own line where
`serve_service(…)` was a single call — the ceremony is what fell.

WHAT TO VERIFY WHEN YOU APPLY IT

1. That the server still boots. `require_shell` REFUSES TO BOOT on a shell
   that does not match the build — that is the point of it, and it is the
   one behavioral change in this patch. Your current `src/app.html` passes
   (verified below), but it will start failing the day the client stops
   emitting styles, which is the intended alarm.
2. `e2e/run.sh` — it drives the real client against a throwaway server, and
   it is the check this draft could not run here (see below). The served
   page is byte-identical to `src/app.html`, so it should be unaffected.
3. `dist/probe.js` still passes: the rpc routes are the same routes.
4. Port 59401 and the `kolt pilot: …` start line are unchanged.

VERIFIED HERE

A scratch copy of `src/` + `vilan.toml` (nothing written back):

  - `vilan check .` exits 0 both before and after the patch, with the shipped
    v0.34.0 CLI and with the current `next` build;
  - `vilan build .` exits 0 and emits client/server/probe;
  - `node dist/server.mjs` boots against a scratch `kolt.db`, and over HTTP:
    `/` → 200 text/html and BYTE-IDENTICAL to `src/app.html`; `/client.js` →
    200 text/javascript; `/client.css` → 200 text/css; `/w/1` (the deep-link
    fallback) → 200 text/html; `POST /rpc` → 200 application/json.

NOT VERIFIED: `e2e/run.sh` (it wants the real checkout), the browser client,
and anything touching your real `kolt.db`.

